  "worked_solution": "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{2}{2x-y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{(2x-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(-\\frac{1}{2x-y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(2x-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(1,-1) & =-\\frac{4}{(2(1)-(-1))^{2}}=-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(1,-1) & =-\\frac{1}{(2(1)-(-1))^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(1,-1)+{g}_{yy}(1,-1)=-\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}=-\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$",
